<title>ITALY: CIR posts 1996 cons net profit after loss.</title>
<headline>CIR posts 1996 cons net profit after loss.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit (loss)	     320    vs   (288.3)</p>
<p>    Parent profit (loss)		 (18.5) vs   (768)</p>
<p>NOTE - Compagnie Industriali Riunite Spa (CIR) is the industrial holding company of Carlo De Benedetti.</p>
<p>CIR said in a statement its consolidated net profit was after extraordinary income of 1.029 trillion lire and after deductions of 499 billion.  </p>
<p>    Cons turnover		    3,795.5    vs  3,639.3</p>
<p>    Cons operating profit	    132.5    vs     42.5</p>
<p>    Cons net equity		  1,252.6    vs    993</p>
<p>    Net financial position (debt)  492	vs (1,601)</p>
<p>Note - CIR Spa said its board had decided not to pay a dividend. It said its consolidated net financial position was 492 billion from which 700 billion would be deducted in April for Cerus to pay foreign shareholders.</p>
<p>It had reduced its holding in information technology group Olivetti and now held a stake of 8.0 percent in the company after 12.8 percent at the end of December 1996.</p>
</text>
